{
  "2Chronicles.16.4.2-c.html": "<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC \"-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.01//EN\" \"http://www.w3.org/TR/html4/strict.dtd\"><HTML>\n<!-- \n     Computer generated from NoteMaker[20 Jan 2026]: \n     Changes file: 2021.10.19 - Changes.xml, date: 2021.08.07, number: 25 .\n     Remove this token \"****COMPUTER-GENERATED****\" if you edit this file manually.\n-->\n<head><meta http-equiv=\"Content-Type\" content=\"text/html; charset=UTF-8\"/>\n  <title>Chronicles_2 16:4.2</title>\n</head>\n<body background=\"../../Images/Background\">\n  <h1>Chronicles_2 16:4.2</h1>\n  <h2>Word lacks accent, add note 'c'; MAM ends the word with a Maqaf (  ס־  ).</h2>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"5pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>\n          <img src=\"../../Changes/2021.10.19 - Changes/images/2021.08.07/25-Detail.jpg\"  border=\"4pt\">\n          </img>\n        </center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>Credit: Sefaria.org.</center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n  <p>\n    <b>\n      <i>Ben Denckla</i>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <p align=\"right\">\n    <b><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Changes/2021.10.19 - Changes/2021.10.19 - Changes.xml?2021.08.07-25\">2021.10.19 - Changes.xml : 2021.08.07-25</a>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"20pt\"  border=\"1pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml?c\">All \"Text is correct relative to LC. Usually this marks a peculiarity of the LC relative to the other Masoretic texts.\" ('c') notes</a></center>\n        </p>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml\">Note index</a></center>\n        </p>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n</body></HTML>",
  "2Chronicles.20.1.2-c.html": "<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC \"-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.01//EN\" \"http://www.w3.org/TR/html4/strict.dtd\"><HTML>\n<!-- \n     Computer generated from NoteMaker[20 Jan 2026]: \n     Changes file: 2023.10.19 - Changes.xml, date: 2023.08.10, number: 1 .\n     Remove this token \"****COMPUTER-GENERATED****\" if you edit this file manually.\n-->\n<head><meta http-equiv=\"Content-Type\" content=\"text/html; charset=UTF-8\"/>\n  <title>Chronicles_2 20:1.2</title>\n</head>\n<body background=\"../../Images/Background\">\n  <h1>Chronicles_2 20:1.2</h1>\n  <h2>Word is usually split with a maqaf between the yod and the kaf.  Add note 'c'.</h2>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"5pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>\n          <img src=\"../../Changes/2023.10.19 - Changes/images/2023.08.10/1-Detail.jpg\"  border=\"4pt\">\n          </img>\n        </center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>Credit: Sefaria.org.</center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n  <p>No space or maqaf is visible between the yod and the kaf.</p>\n  <p>BHL has a maqaf between the yod and the kaf.  BHLA has a space between the yod and the kaf.</p>\n  <p>\n    <b>\n      <i>Dotan BHLA: CVK</i>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <p align=\"right\">\n    <b><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Changes/2023.10.19 - Changes/2023.10.19 - Changes.xml?2023.08.10-1\">2023.10.19 - Changes.xml : 2023.08.10-1</a>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"20pt\"  border=\"1pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml?c\">All \"Text is correct relative to LC. Usually this marks a peculiarity of the LC relative to the other Masoretic texts.\" ('c') notes</a></center>\n        </p>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml\">Note index</a></center>\n        </p>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n</body></HTML>",
  "2Chronicles.20.35.1-c.html": "<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC \"-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.01//EN\" \"http://www.w3.org/TR/html4/strict.dtd\"><HTML>\n<!-- \n     Computer generated from NoteMaker[20 Jan 2026]: \n     Changes file: 2023.10.19 - Changes.xml, date: 2023.08.10, number: 2 .\n     Remove this token \"****COMPUTER-GENERATED****\" if you edit this file manually.\n-->\n<head><meta http-equiv=\"Content-Type\" content=\"text/html; charset=UTF-8\"/>\n  <title>Chronicles_2 20:35.1</title>\n</head>\n<body background=\"../../Images/Background\">\n  <h1>Chronicles_2 20:35.1</h1>\n  <h2>Word usually is split by a maqaf between the yod and the kaf.  Add note 'c'.</h2>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"5pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>\n          <img src=\"../../Changes/2023.10.19 - Changes/images/2023.08.10/2-Detail.jpg\"  border=\"4pt\">\n          </img>\n        </center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>Credit: Sefaria.org.</center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n  <p>No space or maqaf is apparent between the yod and the kaf. A smudge, possibly an erasure, appears under the alef. The  tsere under the kaf is displaced due the presence of the lamed on the following line.</p>\n  <p>BHL has a maqaf between the yod and the kaf.  BHLA has neither a space nor a maqaf between the yod and the kaf.</p>\n  <p>\n    <b>\n      <i>Dotan BHLA: CVK</i>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <p align=\"right\">\n    <b><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Changes/2023.10.19 - Changes/2023.10.19 - Changes.xml?2023.08.10-2\">2023.10.19 - Changes.xml : 2023.08.10-2</a>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"20pt\"  border=\"1pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml?c\">All \"Text is correct relative to LC. Usually this marks a peculiarity of the LC relative to the other Masoretic texts.\" ('c') notes</a></center>\n        </p>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml\">Note index</a></center>\n        </p>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n</body></HTML>",
  "2Chronicles.26.15.18-t.html": "<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC \"-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.01//EN\" \"http://www.w3.org/TR/html4/strict.dtd\"><HTML>\n<!-- \n     Computer generated from NoteMaker[20 Jan 2026]: \n     Changes file: 2023.10.19 - Changes.xml, date: 2023.08.10, number: 8 .\n     Remove this token \"****COMPUTER-GENERATED****\" if you edit this file manually.\n-->\n<head><meta http-equiv=\"Content-Type\" content=\"text/html; charset=UTF-8\"/>\n  <title>Chronicles_2 26:15.18</title>\n</head>\n<body background=\"../../Images/Background\">\n  <h1>Chronicles_2 26:15.18</h1>\n  <h2>Examine possible dagesh in het.  Add note 't'.</h2>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"5pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>\n          <img src=\"../../Changes/2023.10.19 - Changes/images/2023.08.10/8-Detail.jpg\"  border=\"4pt\">\n          </img>\n        </center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>Credit: Sefaria.org.</center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n  <p>A reddish dot appears in the lower center of the het. It is slightly larger than other dots on the page, is lower vertically than expected, but is well-centered horizontally. It will be considered to be an artifact and noted with a 't'.</p>\n  <p>BHL has no dagesh in the het.  BHLA has a dagesh in the het and a '?' in parentheses.</p>\n  <p>\n    <b>\n      <i>Dotan BHLA: CVK</i>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <p align=\"right\">\n    <b><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Changes/2023.10.19 - Changes/2023.10.19 - Changes.xml?2023.08.10-8\">2023.10.19 - Changes.xml : 2023.08.10-8</a>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"20pt\"  border=\"1pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml?t\">All \"Transcription uncertain\" ('t') notes</a></center>\n        </p>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml\">Note index</a></center>\n        </p>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n</body></HTML>",
  "2Chronicles.28.20.10-t.html": "<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC \"-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.01//EN\" \"http://www.w3.org/TR/html4/strict.dtd\"><HTML>\n<!-- \n     Computer generated from NoteMaker[20 Jan 2026]: \n     Changes file: 2024.04.01 - Changes.xml, date: 2023.09.16, number: 16 .\n     Remove this token \"****COMPUTER-GENERATED****\" if you edit this file manually.\n-->\n<head><meta http-equiv=\"Content-Type\" content=\"text/html; charset=UTF-8\"/>\n  <title>Chronicles_2 28:20.10</title>\n</head>\n<body background=\"../../Images/Background\">\n  <h1>Chronicles_2 28:20.10</h1>\n  <h2>Move meteg below the qof to below the zayin. Add note 't'.</h2>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"5pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>\n          <img src=\"../../Changes/2024.04.01 - Changes/images/2023.09.16/16-Detail.jpg\"  border=\"4pt\">\n          </img>\n        </center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>Credit: Sefaria.org.</center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n  <p>The meteg is between the zayin and the qof. Space is available to write the meteg below the qof.</p>\n  <p>BHL has the meteg below the qof.  BHLA has no entry for this verse.</p>\n  <p>\n    <b>\n      <i>Daniel Holman</i>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <p align=\"right\">\n    <b><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Changes/2024.04.01 - Changes/2024.04.01 - Changes.xml?2023.09.16-16\">2024.04.01 - Changes.xml : 2023.09.16-16</a>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"20pt\"  border=\"1pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml?t\">All \"Transcription uncertain\" ('t') notes</a></center>\n        </p>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml\">Note index</a></center>\n        </p>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n</body></HTML>",
  "2Chronicles.29.28.7-y.html": "<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC \"-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.01//EN\" \"http://www.w3.org/TR/html4/strict.dtd\"><HTML>\n<!-- \n     Computer generated from NoteMaker[20 Jan 2026]: \n     Changes file: 2024.10.19 - Changes.xml, date: 2024.07.08, number: 33 .\n     Remove this token \"****COMPUTER-GENERATED****\" if you edit this file manually.\n-->\n<head><meta http-equiv=\"Content-Type\" content=\"text/html; charset=UTF-8\"/>\n  <title>Chronicles_2 29:28.7</title>\n</head>\n<body background=\"../../Images/Background\">\n  <h1>Chronicles_2 29:28.7</h1>\n  <h2>Add transcription note 'y' to yatir ketiv word. (yatir tsadi)</h2>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"5pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>\n          <img src=\"../../Changes/2024.10.19 - Changes/images/2024.07.08/33-Detail.jpg\"  border=\"4pt\">\n          </img>\n        </center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>Credit: Sefaria.org.</center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n  <p>The yatir marking for this word is the left margin; it is a yatir tsadi. Two words with Masorah circles appear in the line for only one yatir tsadi note; the preceding word and this word. Both tsadis in the preceeding word are vowelized; thus, this word is the object of the yatir tsadi note. The second tsadi in this word is unvowelized and unaccented; that tsadi the yatir will be applied to that letter (not that it matters which tsadi is taken).</p>\n  <p>BHL has a qere/ketiv pair for this word; the qere word has a single tsadi. (The previous word has no qere/ketiv pair and has double tsadis. BHLA has no entry for this verse.</p>\n  <p>\n    <b>\n      <i>CVK</i>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <p align=\"right\">\n    <b><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Changes/2024.10.19 - Changes/2024.10.19 - Changes.xml?2024.07.08-33\">2024.10.19 - Changes.xml : 2024.07.08-33</a>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"20pt\"  border=\"1pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml?y\">All \"Yatir: The preceding Hebrew letter is \"superfluous\".\" ('y') notes</a></center>\n        </p>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml\">Note index</a></center>\n        </p>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n</body></HTML>",
  "2Chronicles.30.11.8-c.html": "<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC \"-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.01//EN\" \"http://www.w3.org/TR/html4/strict.dtd\"><HTML>\n<!-- \n     Computer generated from NoteMaker[20 Jan 2026]: \n     Changes file: 2023.10.19 - Changes.xml, date: 2023.08.10, number: 11 .\n     Remove this token \"****COMPUTER-GENERATED****\" if you edit this file manually.\n-->\n<head><meta http-equiv=\"Content-Type\" content=\"text/html; charset=UTF-8\"/>\n  <title>Chronicles_2 30:11.8</title>\n</head>\n<body background=\"../../Images/Background\">\n  <h1>Chronicles_2 30:11.8</h1>\n  <h2>Change qamats below shin to hataf-qamats. Add note 'c'.</h2>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"5pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>\n          <img src=\"../../Changes/2023.10.19 - Changes/images/2023.08.10/11-Detail.jpg\"  border=\"4pt\">\n          </img>\n        </center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>Credit: Sefaria.org.</center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n  <p>A sheva is apparent below the shin before the qamats suggesting a hataf-qamats. This is very unusual.</p>\n  <p>BHL has no sheva under the shin.  BHLA has a hataf-qamats under the shin.</p>\n  <p>\n    <b>\n      <i>Dotan BHLA: CVK</i>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <p align=\"right\">\n    <b><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Changes/2023.10.19 - Changes/2023.10.19 - Changes.xml?2023.08.10-11\">2023.10.19 - Changes.xml : 2023.08.10-11</a>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"20pt\"  border=\"1pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml?c\">All \"Text is correct relative to LC. Usually this marks a peculiarity of the LC relative to the other Masoretic texts.\" ('c') notes</a></center>\n        </p>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml\">Note index</a></center>\n        </p>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n</body></HTML>",
  "2Chronicles.31.12.9-y.html": "<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC \"-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.01//EN\" \"http://www.w3.org/TR/html4/strict.dtd\"><HTML>\n<!-- \n     Computer generated from NoteMaker[20 Jan 2026]: \n     Changes file: 2024.10.19 - Changes.xml, date: 2024.07.08, number: 34 .\n     Remove this token \"****COMPUTER-GENERATED****\" if you edit this file manually.\n-->\n<head><meta http-equiv=\"Content-Type\" content=\"text/html; charset=UTF-8\"/>\n  <title>Chronicles_2 31:12.9</title>\n</head>\n<body background=\"../../Images/Background\">\n  <h1>Chronicles_2 31:12.9</h1>\n  <h2>Add transcription note 'y' to yatir ketiv word. (yatir vav)</h2>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"5pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>\n          <img src=\"../../Changes/2024.10.19 - Changes/images/2024.07.08/34-Detail.jpg\"  border=\"4pt\">\n          </img>\n        </center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>Credit: Sefaria.org.</center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n  <p>The yatir vav marking is in the left margin and is very light. A Masorah circle is present over this word and the first vav is unvowelized and unaccented. The yatir will be applied to the first vav.</p>\n  <p>BHL has a qere/ketiv pair for this word; it has no vav between the kaf and the nun.  BHLA has no entry for this verse.</p>\n  <p>\n    <b>\n      <i>CVK</i>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <p align=\"right\">\n    <b><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Changes/2024.10.19 - Changes/2024.10.19 - Changes.xml?2024.07.08-34\">2024.10.19 - Changes.xml : 2024.07.08-34</a>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"20pt\"  border=\"1pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml?y\">All \"Yatir: The preceding Hebrew letter is \"superfluous\".\" ('y') notes</a></center>\n        </p>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml\">Note index</a></center>\n        </p>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n</body></HTML>",
  "2Chronicles.31.13.13-y.html": "<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC \"-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.01//EN\" \"http://www.w3.org/TR/html4/strict.dtd\"><HTML>\n<!-- \n     Computer generated from NoteMaker[20 Jan 2026]: \n     Changes file: 2024.10.19 - Changes.xml, date: 2024.07.08, number: 35 .\n     Remove this token \"****COMPUTER-GENERATED****\" if you edit this file manually.\n-->\n<head><meta http-equiv=\"Content-Type\" content=\"text/html; charset=UTF-8\"/>\n  <title>Chronicles_2 31:13.13</title>\n</head>\n<body background=\"../../Images/Background\">\n  <h1>Chronicles_2 31:13.13</h1>\n  <h2>Add transcription note 'y' to yatir ketiv word. (yatir vav)</h2>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"5pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>\n          <img src=\"../../Changes/2024.10.19 - Changes/images/2024.07.08/35-Detail.jpg\"  border=\"4pt\">\n          </img>\n        </center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>Credit: Sefaria.org.</center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n  <p>The yatir marking for this word is in the left margin; it is a yatir vav and is light. \n\t\t\t\t\t\tThis word has no Masorah circle; however, the first vav in this word is the only unmarked vav on the line. \n\t\t\t\t\t\tThe yatir vav will be applied to the first vav.\n\t\t\t\t\t\tWLC 4.20 lacks a 'y' transcription note for this word.</p>\n  <p>BHL has a qere/ketiv pair for this word; the qere word has no vav between the kaf and the nun.  BHLA has no entry for this verse.</p>\n  <p>\n    <b>\n      <i>CVK</i>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <p align=\"right\">\n    <b><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Changes/2024.10.19 - Changes/2024.10.19 - Changes.xml?2024.07.08-35\">2024.10.19 - Changes.xml : 2024.07.08-35</a>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"20pt\"  border=\"1pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml?y\">All \"Yatir: The preceding Hebrew letter is \"superfluous\".\" ('y') notes</a></center>\n        </p>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml\">Note index</a></center>\n        </p>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n</body></HTML>",
  "2Chronicles.32.12.16-t.html": "<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC \"-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.01//EN\" \"http://www.w3.org/TR/html4/strict.dtd\"><HTML>\n<!-- \n     Computer generated from NoteMaker[20 Jan 2026]: \n     Changes file: 2023.10.19 - Changes.xml, date: 2023.08.10, number: 13 .\n     Remove this token \"****COMPUTER-GENERATED****\" if you edit this file manually.\n-->\n<head><meta http-equiv=\"Content-Type\" content=\"text/html; charset=UTF-8\"/>\n  <title>Chronicles_2 32:12.16</title>\n</head>\n<body background=\"../../Images/Background\">\n  <h1>Chronicles_2 32:12.16</h1>\n  <h2>Add dagesh to first vav. Add note 't'.</h2>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"5pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>\n          <img src=\"../../Changes/2023.10.19 - Changes/images/2023.08.10/13-Detail.jpg\"  border=\"4pt\">\n          </img>\n        </center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>Credit: Sefaria.org.</center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n  <p>A dagesh is visible in the first vav although it is attached to the shaft of the vav. It is well-positioned vertically.</p>\n  <p>BHL has no dagesh in the first vav.  BHLA has a dagesh in the first vav.</p>\n  <p>\n    <b>\n      <i>Dotan BHLA: CVK</i>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <p align=\"right\">\n    <b><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Changes/2023.10.19 - Changes/2023.10.19 - Changes.xml?2023.08.10-13\">2023.10.19 - Changes.xml : 2023.08.10-13</a>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"20pt\"  border=\"1pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml?t\">All \"Transcription uncertain\" ('t') notes</a></center>\n        </p>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml\">Note index</a></center>\n        </p>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n</body></HTML>",
  "2Chronicles.34.25.4-y.html": "<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC \"-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.01//EN\" \"http://www.w3.org/TR/html4/strict.dtd\"><HTML>\n<!-- \n     Computer generated from NoteMaker[20 Jan 2026]: \n     Changes file: 2024.10.19 - Changes.xml, date: 2024.07.08, number: 36 .\n     Remove this token \"****COMPUTER-GENERATED****\" if you edit this file manually.\n-->\n<head><meta http-equiv=\"Content-Type\" content=\"text/html; charset=UTF-8\"/>\n  <title>Chronicles_2 34:25.4</title>\n</head>\n<body background=\"../../Images/Background\">\n  <h1>Chronicles_2 34:25.4</h1>\n  <h2>Add transcription note 'y' to yatir ketiv word. (yatir yod)</h2>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"5pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>\n          <img src=\"../../Changes/2024.10.19 - Changes/images/2024.07.08/36-Detail.jpg\"  border=\"4pt\">\n          </img>\n        </center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>Credit: Sefaria.org.</center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n  <p>The yatir marking for this word is the right margin; it is a yatir yod. \n\t\t\t\t\t\tThe word has two yods; the first is vowelized, the second is unvowelized and unaccented. \n\t\t\t\t\t\tThe second yod will be marked as the yatir yod. \n\t\t\t\t\t\t</p>\n  <p>BHL has a qere/ketiv pair for this word; the qere word has no yod between the tet and the resh.  BHLA has no entry for this verse.</p>\n  <p>\n    <b>\n      <i>CVK</i>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <p align=\"right\">\n    <b><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Changes/2024.10.19 - Changes/2024.10.19 - Changes.xml?2024.07.08-36\">2024.10.19 - Changes.xml : 2024.07.08-36</a>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"20pt\"  border=\"1pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml?y\">All \"Yatir: The preceding Hebrew letter is \"superfluous\".\" ('y') notes</a></center>\n        </p>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml\">Note index</a></center>\n        </p>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n</body></HTML>",
  "2Chronicles.36.10.5-t.html": "<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC \"-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.01//EN\" \"http://www.w3.org/TR/html4/strict.dtd\"><HTML>\n<!-- \n     Computer generated from NoteMaker[20 Jan 2026]: \n     Changes file: 2024.04.01 - Changes.xml, date: 2023.09.16, number: 23 .\n     Remove this token \"****COMPUTER-GENERATED****\" if you edit this file manually.\n-->\n<head><meta http-equiv=\"Content-Type\" content=\"text/html; charset=UTF-8\"/>\n  <title>Chronicles_2 36:10.5</title>\n</head>\n<body background=\"../../Images/Background\">\n  <h1>Chronicles_2 36:10.5</h1>\n  <h2>Remove dagesh from tsadi. Add note 't'.</h2>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"5pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>\n          <img src=\"../../Changes/2024.04.01 - Changes/images/2023.09.16/23-Detail.jpg\"  border=\"4pt\">\n          </img>\n        </center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>Credit: Sefaria.org.</center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n  <p>The word נבוכדנאצר normally has a dagesh in the tsadi.  The dagesh is usually placed below the upper arms of the tsadi as displayed in the modern font. Here the tsadi has a reddish blob in between its upper arms. The blob is larger than expected and positioned too far to the left. A dagesh will not be transcribed in the tsadi; however, a note 't' will be added.</p>\n  <p>BHL has a dagesh in the tsadi.  BHLA has no entry for this verse.</p>\n  <p>\n    <b>\n      <i>Daniel Holman</i>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <p align=\"right\">\n    <b><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Changes/2024.04.01 - Changes/2024.04.01 - Changes.xml?2023.09.16-23\">2024.04.01 - Changes.xml : 2023.09.16-23</a>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"20pt\"  border=\"1pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml?t\">All \"Transcription uncertain\" ('t') notes</a></center>\n        </p>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml\">Note index</a></center>\n        </p>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n</body></HTML>",
  "2Chronicles.6.29.12-t.html": "<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC \"-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.01//EN\" \"http://www.w3.org/TR/html4/strict.dtd\"><HTML>\n<!-- \n     Computer generated from NoteMaker[20 Jan 2026]: \n     Changes file: 2024.04.01 - Changes.xml, date: 2023.09.16, number: 2 .\n     Remove this token \"****COMPUTER-GENERATED****\" if you edit this file manually.\n-->\n<head><meta http-equiv=\"Content-Type\" content=\"text/html; charset=UTF-8\"/>\n  <title>Chronicles_2 6:29.12</title>\n</head>\n<body background=\"../../Images/Background\">\n  <h1>Chronicles_2 6:29.12</h1>\n  <h2>Add meteg between sheva and patah under the alef. Add ZWJ to force visual ordering to match LC. Add note 't'.</h2>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"5pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>\n          <img src=\"../../Changes/2024.04.01 - Changes/images/2023.09.16/2-Detail.jpg\"  border=\"4pt\">\n          </img>\n        </center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>Credit: Sefaria.org.</center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n  <p>A slightly curved mark occurs between the sheva and the patah.  The comma-like shape of the meteg is a very unusual. The markings below the alef probably mean a hataf-patah vowel with a meteg accent. Other instances of a meteg 'splitting' a hataf vowel occur in the LC.</p>\n  <p>BHL has sheva, then meteg, then patah under the alef.  BHLA has no entry for this verse.</p>\n  <p>\n    <b>\n      <i>Daniel Holman</i>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <p align=\"right\">\n    <b><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Changes/2024.04.01 - Changes/2024.04.01 - Changes.xml?2023.09.16-2\">2024.04.01 - Changes.xml : 2023.09.16-2</a>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"20pt\"  border=\"1pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml?t\">All \"Transcription uncertain\" ('t') notes</a></center>\n        </p>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml\">Note index</a></center>\n        </p>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n</body></HTML>",
  "2Chronicles.8.10.3-t.html": "<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC \"-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.01//EN\" \"http://www.w3.org/TR/html4/strict.dtd\"><HTML>\n<!-- \n     Computer generated from NoteMaker[20 Jan 2026]: \n     Changes file: 2024.10.19 - Changes.xml, date: 2024.07.08, number: 32 .\n     Remove this token \"****COMPUTER-GENERATED****\" if you edit this file manually.\n-->\n<head><meta http-equiv=\"Content-Type\" content=\"text/html; charset=UTF-8\"/>\n  <title>Chronicles_2 8:10.3</title>\n</head>\n<body background=\"../../Images/Background\">\n  <h1>Chronicles_2 8:10.3</h1>\n  <h2>Add transcription note 'y' to yatir ketiv word. (yatir yod) Add note 't' for ambiquity.</h2>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"5pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>\n          <img src=\"../../Changes/2024.10.19 - Changes/images/2024.07.08/32-Detail.jpg\"  border=\"4pt\">\n          </img>\n        </center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>Credit: Sefaria.org.</center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n  <p>The yatir marking for this word is the left margin; it is a yatir yod. The word has two unvowelized and unaccented yods; the first yod will be taken as the yatir. A note 't' is added for the ambiquity.</p>\n  <p>BHL has a qere/ketiv pair for this word; the qere word has no yod between the tsadi and the bet.  BHLA has no entry for this verse.</p>\n  <p>\n    <b>\n      <i>CVK</i>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <p align=\"right\">\n    <b><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Changes/2024.10.19 - Changes/2024.10.19 - Changes.xml?2024.07.08-32\">2024.10.19 - Changes.xml : 2024.07.08-32</a>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"20pt\"  border=\"1pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml?t\">All \"Transcription uncertain\" ('t') notes</a></center>\n        </p>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml\">Note index</a></center>\n        </p>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n</body></HTML>",
  "2Chronicles.8.10.3-y.html": "<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC \"-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.01//EN\" \"http://www.w3.org/TR/html4/strict.dtd\"><HTML>\n<!-- \n     Computer generated from NoteMaker[20 Jan 2026]: \n     Changes file: 2024.10.19 - Changes.xml, date: 2024.07.08, number: 32 .\n     Remove this token \"****COMPUTER-GENERATED****\" if you edit this file manually.\n-->\n<head><meta http-equiv=\"Content-Type\" content=\"text/html; charset=UTF-8\"/>\n  <title>Chronicles_2 8:10.3</title>\n</head>\n<body background=\"../../Images/Background\">\n  <h1>Chronicles_2 8:10.3</h1>\n  <h2>Add transcription note 'y' to yatir ketiv word. (yatir yod) Add note 't' for ambiquity.</h2>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"5pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>\n          <img src=\"../../Changes/2024.10.19 - Changes/images/2024.07.08/32-Detail.jpg\"  border=\"4pt\">\n          </img>\n        </center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>Credit: Sefaria.org.</center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n  <p>The yatir marking for this word is the left margin; it is a yatir yod. The word has two unvowelized and unaccented yods; the first yod will be taken as the yatir. A note 't' is added for the ambiquity.</p>\n  <p>BHL has a qere/ketiv pair for this word; the qere word has no yod between the tsadi and the bet.  BHLA has no entry for this verse.</p>\n  <p>\n    <b>\n      <i>CVK</i>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <p align=\"right\">\n    <b><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Changes/2024.10.19 - Changes/2024.10.19 - Changes.xml?2024.07.08-32\">2024.10.19 - Changes.xml : 2024.07.08-32</a>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"20pt\"  border=\"1pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml?y\">All \"Yatir: The preceding Hebrew letter is \"superfluous\".\" ('y') notes</a></center>\n        </p>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml\">Note index</a></center>\n        </p>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n</body></HTML>",
  "2Chronicles.8.11.26-t.html": "<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC \"-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.01//EN\" \"http://www.w3.org/TR/html4/strict.dtd\"><HTML>\n<!-- \n     Computer generated from NoteMaker[20 Jan 2026]: \n     Changes file: 2024.04.01 - Changes.xml, date: 2023.09.16, number: 5 .\n     Remove this token \"****COMPUTER-GENERATED****\" if you edit this file manually.\n-->\n<head><meta http-equiv=\"Content-Type\" content=\"text/html; charset=UTF-8\"/>\n  <title>Chronicles_2 8:11.26</title>\n</head>\n<body background=\"../../Images/Background\">\n  <h1>Chronicles_2 8:11.26</h1>\n  <h2>Accents under the bet and alef are uncertain. Add note 't'.</h2>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"5pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>\n          <img src=\"../../Changes/2024.04.01 - Changes/images/2023.09.16/5-Detail.jpg\"  border=\"4pt\">\n          </img>\n        </center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>Credit: Sefaria.org.</center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n  <p>Both the bet and alef have vertical bars under them. The bar under the alef is significantly longer.  Generally, this would indicate that the bar under the alef is a merkha as in the present text.  (This is in contrast to BHL which has a meteg under the alef.)</p>\n  <p>BHL has a merkha under the bet and a meteg under the alef.  BHLA has no entry for this verse.</p>\n  <p>\n    <b>\n      <i>Daniel Holman</i>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <p align=\"right\">\n    <b><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Changes/2024.04.01 - Changes/2024.04.01 - Changes.xml?2023.09.16-5\">2024.04.01 - Changes.xml : 2023.09.16-5</a>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"20pt\"  border=\"1pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml?t\">All \"Transcription uncertain\" ('t') notes</a></center>\n        </p>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml\">Note index</a></center>\n        </p>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n</body></HTML>"
}
